THOUGHT 1: The detection call raised an exception (likely an upstream API/timeout returning None). I'll make the code robust by wrapping detection and segmentation calls in try/except blocks. If detection fails, I'll fall back to sliding_window_detection to search for "ball". I'll also attempt segmentation (in a safe try/except) to get region proposals. The code will display whatever annotated outputs succeed and print clear diagnostic messages and bounding boxes so we can continue the analysis.

